From: Zenith
Subject: [PATCH] ES: wait for the ROMs mount (ES_WAIT_ROMS_READY) just before scanning systems so ES startup overlaps rocknix-automount

In the early boot essway no longer waits for rocknix-automount.service; ES starts at once and waits (max 15 s) for the ready file
right before loadSystemConfigFile, when it actually needs the ROMs.
---
--- a/es-app/src/main.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/main.cpp
@@ -611,6 +611,20 @@
 		TextureData::PdfHandler = ApiSystem::getInstance();
 	
 	threadPool->waitAllExcept(vlcInit); // Wait for what's necessary for loadSystemConfigFile
+	// Zenith: arranque temprano. Si start_es.sh exporta ES_WAIT_ROMS_READY, rocknix-automount puede seguir montando las ROMs mientras
+	// ES arranca; aqui se espera (max 15 s) a que cree ese fichero justo antes de escanear los sistemas.
+#ifndef WIN32
+	{
+		const char* waitRoms = getenv("ES_WAIT_ROMS_READY");
+		if (waitRoms != nullptr && *waitRoms != 0)
+		{
+			struct stat romsSt;
+			for (int w = 0; w < 750 && stat(waitRoms, &romsSt) != 0; w++)
+				usleep(20000);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
 
 	const char* errorMsg = NULL;
 	if (!loadSystemConfigFile(splashScreen && splashScreenProgress ? &window : nullptr, &errorMsg))
